{"chapter": "stacks-properties", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "04XE", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$K$", "MATH_0002": "$L$", "MATH_0003": "$\\Spec(K) \\to \\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\Spec(L) \\to \\mathcal{Z}$", "MATH_0005": "$|\\mathcal{Y}|$", "MATH_0006": "$M/K$", "MATH_0007": "$M/L$", "MATH_0008": "$\\Spec(M) \\to \\Spec(K) \\to \\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0009": "$\\Spec(M) \\to \\Spec(L) \\to \\mathcal{Z} \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0010": "$2$", "MATH_0011": "$\\Spec(M) \\to \\mathcal{Z} \\times_\\mathcal{Y} \\mathcal{X}$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:2f7e54c1c6b844fab39933de9047981c824ae28edfcf21db9df8d5004924be97", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:0828c9c08131f2d980b224b79ecbf736a3dd9745dc29d52ad3c5ab004a3f37a2", "source_text": "Namely, suppose given fields <MATH_0001>, <MATH_0002> and morphisms\n<MATH_0003>, <MATH_0004>,\nthen the assumption that they agree as elements of <MATH_0005> means that\nthere is a common extension <MATH_0006> and <MATH_0007>\nsuch that\n<MATH_0008> and\n<MATH_0009>\nare <MATH_0010>-isomorphic. And this is exactly the condition which says you get a\nmorphism <MATH_0011>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:2b40d025395080a422c69d89dd58dbc89f60bb1cc272b4fff9aeaf5bafbd3a26", "unit_id": "tag:04XH:proof"}
{"chapter": "stacks-properties", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "04XE", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : \\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0002": "$|f| : |\\mathcal{X}| \\to |\\mathcal{Y}|$", "MATH_0003": "$f$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{section-properties-morphisms}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-characterize-surjective}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:947e5ca6695ae412f2a6e3a434cefc95cd7474e40b525a54e8f9f54a3c062b63", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:e1bfa197384515930f2e1853b163ac759507311b810d0da6303ee1afb5e601b3", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a morphism of algebraic stacks\nwhich is representable by algebraic spaces. The following are equivalent:\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> <MATH_0002> is surjective, and\n<STRUCT_0003> <MATH_0003> is surjective\n(in the sense of Section <REF_0001>).\n<STRUCT_0004>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:dab04e6e347a47ba964a44e5d4d08389c1ff386eaf8affc1fb3dd8683faff975", "unit_id": "tag:04XI:statement"}
{"chapter": "stacks-properties", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "04XE", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$T \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0002": "$T \\times_\\mathcal{Y} \\mathcal{X} \\to T$", "MATH_0003": "$|T \\times_\\mathcal{Y} \\mathcal{X}| \\to |T|$", "MATH_0004": "$y : \\Spec(K) \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0006": "$\\Spec(K) \\times_{y, \\mathcal{Y}} \\mathcal{X} \\to \\Spec(K)$", "MATH_0007": "$K'/K$", "MATH_0008": "$\\Spec(K') \\to \\Spec(K) \\times_{y, \\mathcal{Y}} \\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0009": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\n\\Spec(K') \\ar[r] \\ar[d] &\n\\Spec(K) \\times_{y, \\mathcal{Y}} \\mathcal{X} \\ar[d] \\ar[r] &\n\\mathcal{X} \\ar[d]\n\\\\\n\\Spec(K) \\ar@{=}[r] &\n\\Spec(K) \\ar[r]^-y &\n\\mathcal{Y}\n}\n$$", "MATH_0010": "$|X| \\to |\\mathcal{Y}|$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{spaces-morphisms-definition-surjective}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-points-cartesian}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{spaces-morphisms-definition-surjective}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0002": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:ed51e12e557f17d93192a61443625e1d260df6cb8e39499701453467ad6ad96e", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:468e449aef2c35d386c540fa8761d895ac0fd962fc9b88c5e20d9847200d0748", "source_text": "Assume (1). Let <MATH_0001> be a morphism whose source is a scheme.\nTo prove (2) we have to show that the morphism of algebraic spaces\n<MATH_0002> is surjective. By\nMorphisms of Spaces, Definition <REF_0001>\nthis means we have to show that\n<MATH_0003> is surjective.\nApplying\nLemma <REF_0002>\nwe see that this follows from (1).\n\n<STRUCT_0001><STRUCT_0002>\nConversely, assume (2). Let <MATH_0004> be a\nmorphism from the spectrum of a field into <MATH_0005>. By assumption the\nmorphism\n<MATH_0006>\nof algebraic spaces is surjective. By\nMorphisms of Spaces, Definition <REF_0003>\nthis means there exists a field extension\n<MATH_0007> and a morphism\n<MATH_0008>\nsuch that the left square of the diagram\n<MATH_0009>\nis commutative. This shows that <MATH_0010> is surjective.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:6bb7c3cfde32a10574aaf44e1b22586c23c98ace78c34ea40abfa8e2d5c28552", "unit_id": "tag:04XI:proof"}
